DESCRIPTION:Long-running (6th edition\, since 2015) small-format geroscienc
 e conference on molecular/cellular mechanisms of aging and translation int
 o human interventions – exercise\, chronobiology\, tissue-specific aging
  biomarkers\, genetic variation\, and systems biology approaches to health
 y aging.\n\nWhy it matters for mTOR (★★): Core geroscience meeting cha
 ired by leading nutrient-sensing/aging researchers (Linda Partridge\, Hein
 rich Jasper\, William Mair – all with major contributions to TOR/insulin
 -IGF1 longevity pathway work)\; sessions on pharmacological and lifestyle 
 interventions targeting core aging mechanisms directly overlap the Atlas's
  mTOR/geroscience scope. Rapamycin/mTOR inhibition is a recurring theme in
  aging-intervention pharmacology alongside adjacent biology\, as at ARDD.\
